{
  "about": "Canvas `font` shorthands and what each sets. Read by tests/css_grammar.rs for the Rust font grammar and by tests/suite/css-grammar.test.js for `ctx.font`, so the two surfaces answer one table rather than two.",
  "source": "Chrome 152.0.7977.149: ctx.font set on a fresh 2D context after a sentinel font, then ctx.font, ctx.fontVariantCaps and ctx.fontStretch read back, measured 2026-10-22. A refused row is one Chrome ignored, leaving the sentinel. `parts` is Chrome's serialized font taken apart; `lineHeight`, which Chrome does not expose, is CSS Fonts 4's: a number or percentage multiplies the size, `normal` is none. Relative sizes resolve against the canvas's default 10px font and `rem` against 16px, as Chrome does.",
  "notMeasured": "System-font keywords (caption, icon, menu, message-box, small-caption, status-bar) and `oblique 10deg 16px Arial` are left out: Chrome on macOS read every system font as 16px Arial, which is platform-specific, and serialized the oblique angle away.",
  "knownDifferences": "Measured and left out, because neither surface matches Chrome yet: `2ex Arial` and `1ch Arial`, which Chrome resolves against its default face (8.97461px and 5px on macOS) and both surfaces refuse; and `16px \"serif\"` and `16px \"inherit\"`, which Chrome keeps quoted because a quoted generic or keyword names a family literally, and which a `Font` cannot tell from the unquoted name.",
